                    "id": "m2-c1b1",
                    "type": "text",
                    "data": {
                      "html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;font-size:13px;color:#504442;line-height:1.75;font-family:'Manrope',Arial,sans-serif;\">High in the Ethiopian highlands, at altitudes above 1,900 metres, the air carries the scent of wild jasmine and damp volcanic earth. It is here — in the ancient forest gardens of the Gedeo Zone — that our Yirgacheffe coffee is grown under a dense canopy of shade trees, nurtured by generations of smallholder farmers.</p><p style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#504442;line-height:1.75;font-family:'Manrope',Arial,sans-serif;\">The unique terroir of this region, defined by rich red clay soils and a cool, misty microclimate, imparts a vivid floral complexity to every bean. Each harvest is hand-selected at peak ripeness, then carefully washed in mountain spring water — a process that locks in brightness and clarity, letting the origin speak without compromise.</p>",
                      "variables": []
                    },
                    "style": {
